/target

# Not tracked on purpose, as in the rest of the family: the toolkit is the
# dependency that moves, and every engine here builds against it as it stands
# rather than against a frozen revision.
Cargo.lock

# The checkpoints the engine reads are converted .safetensors files; the
# upstream .pt originals are large and are not part of this project. The
# de-light-effects one is a zip container and the LOL one is a legacy pickle,
# so both extensions are listed.
*.pt
*.pth

# Python: tools/ has two scripts, and running them leaves bytecode behind.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# The files staged for a release, and the release body: they are built from the
# tree and attached to GitHub, not committed to it.
release-assets/
release-notes.md
